---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL

// Price points are Odysseus's (ARC-1 plan). Copy is a placeholder for Hermes.
const plans = [
  {
    name: 'Free',
    price: '€0',
    per: 'forever',
    limit: '100 requests / day',
    for: 'Trying it, and small internal tools.',
    features: ['Full obligation rows', 'Source URL and checked-on date', 'No card required'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Starter',
    price: '€39',
    per: 'per month',
    limit: '10,000 requests / day',
    for: 'One product that needs the matrix.',
    features: ['Everything in Free', 'Change alerts by email', 'CSV snapshot export'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Vendor',
    price: '€99',
    per: 'per month',
    limit: '100,000 requests / day',
    for: 'Accounting and ERP vendors shipping to EU customers.',
    features: ['Everything in Starter', 'Webhook on every dataset change', 'Changelog diffs per row'],
  },
]
---
<Base
  title="Pricing | EU E-Invoicing Deadlines API"
  description="Free tier with 100 requests a day. €39/month for 10,000 a day with change alerts, €99/month for 100,000 a day with webhooks. No card needed to start."
>
  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The checker pages are free and always will be. You pay for the same data as JSON, kept current,
    with a webhook when it changes.
  </p>

  <ul class="plans">
    {plans.map((p) => (
      <li class="plan">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">{p.name}</h2>
        <span class="price">{p.price}</span>
        <span class="muted">{p.per}</span>
        <p><strong>{p.limit}</strong></p>
        <p class="muted">{p.for}</p>
        <ul>{p.features.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}</ul>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Self-serve signup is not open yet.</strong> The API, the keys and the rate limits are
    built and running; the payment account is the one piece still missing, so there is no checkout
    button here rather than a button that does not work. Free-tier keys are issued on request in
    the meantime.
  </div>

  <h2>What counts as a request</h2>
  <p>
    One HTTP call to a <code>/v1/</code> endpoint. Limits are per key, per rolling day, and they
    are enforced from the first deploy &mdash; you will get a <code>429</code> with a
    <code>Retry-After</code> header, not a surprise invoice.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions you are entitled to ask first</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>How current is it?</strong> Every row carries a <code>checked_on</code> date. Look at it before you buy.</li>
    <li><strong>What happens when a date moves?</strong> It becomes a dated entry in the changelog, and on paid plans a webhook. The diff is the product.</li>
    <li><strong>Can I see it first?</strong> Yes. The free tier returns full rows, not a teaser.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><a href={`${base}docs/`}>Read the API docs &rarr;</a></p>
</Base>
